# [P1] Lemma 14, (HX), second equality (j = 1, n = 1 input, m = 2 outputs, d = 3): the green K_j
# spider is v_{m,n} times the pink K_{d-j} spider with H^dagger on its input and H on its outputs.
# Dimensions are literal. Paper pink spiders are X spiders with their normalisation d^((m+n)/2 - 1) as scalar.

@lhs =
    z = Z(1 -> 2, literal 3) phase{k: k/3}

@rhs =
    a = F(literal 3); x = X(1 -> 2, literal 3) phase{k: 2*k/3}; a -> F(literal 3)^2 -> x
    x -> F(literal 3); x -> F(literal 3)
    scalar 3^(1/2) * 3^(-1/2)

load @lhs
prove against @rhs
certificate kernel
